// =============================================================================
// STSH Shielded Pool Canister
// Security classification: ESCROW BOUNDARY
// =============================================================================
//
// DESIGN DOCTRINE: Private transactions, public solvency.
//
// THIS CANISTER:
//   - Holds public STSH as escrow (deposited via ICRC-2)
//   - Creates/spends private notes backed by that escrow
//   - NEVER mints new STSH
//   - NEVER credits shielded balances without a prior public deposit
//   - NEVER accesses treasury subaccounts (fee revenue goes TO treasury, not from it)
//
// NON-NEGOTIABLE SOLVENCY INVARIANTS (M3 — 6-bucket accounting model):
//
//   (1) escrow_backing + pending_fee_reimbursements >= private_liability
//       The pool always holds enough public STSH to honour all outstanding notes,
//       even when a reimbursement from the operations reserve is in-flight.
//
//   (2) operations_reserve >= pending_fee_reimbursements
//       The operations reserve must be able to cover all pending reimbursements.
//       Violation here is a governance alert — top up the operations reserve.
//
//   Legacy form (still true):
//   total_withdrawable_private_value <= public_STSH_escrow_balance
//
// SUPPLY-BOUNDARY LESSON (June 2026):
//   A circuit soundness bug could allow invalid state transitions.
//   Mitigation: circuit versioning on every proof, pinned VK, governance-timelocked upgrades.
//
// WITHDRAWAL FLOW uses an idempotent state machine to prevent:
//   - Double-execution of the same withdrawal
//   - Nullifier reuse after a failed transfer
//   - Reentrancy via inter-canister calls
// =============================================================================

