/// activation (the lazy time-gated swap in `maybe_activate_pending_vk`),
/// successful `set_verifier_canister`, and spend pause/unpause. Fee/params
/// changes are deliberately NOT epoch events — they are snapshotted per-spend
/// and must never abort an in-flight spend. NOT a structural snapshot (ABA-
/// vulnerable: pause→unpause or verifier A→B→A returns an identical structure
/// while a real change occurred). Deliberately NOT in `PoolStableState` (same
/// pattern as the P-ROOT cells): the cell survives upgrade on its own, so no
/// `STATE_VERSION` bump.
const MEM_SECURITY_EPOCH: MemoryId = MemoryId::new(16);

/// A-1 (RB-SWARM-A1): EAGER cell holding the fee-governance control state —
