/// is precisely that they move together or not at all. One `Cell::set` makes a
/// half-applied governance record (say, a bumped epoch with a stale cooldown
/// clock, or an activation marker without its timestamp) unrepresentable.
///
/// Why these live OUTSIDE `PoolStableState`: the same reason as the P-ROOT and
/// P-VK cells. They are the authority for a security-relevant clock, and a
/// clock that only becomes durable at `pre_upgrade` is a clock an aborted
/// upgrade can rewind. Eager, fail-closed, and independent of the checkpoint.
const MEM_FEE_GOVERNANCE: MemoryId = MemoryId::new(18);

/// FU1-2 (lane A-5) — the six accounting scalars, EAGER.
