const ACCT_W_PRIVATE_LIABILITY: usize = 0;
const ACCT_W_ESCROW_BACKING: usize = 1;
const ACCT_W_OPERATIONS_RESERVE: usize = 2;
const ACCT_W_INSURANCE_RESERVE: usize = 3;
const ACCT_W_GOVERNANCE_REWARDS_RESERVE: usize = 4;
const ACCT_W_PENDING_FEE_REIMBURSEMENTS: usize = 5;

/// FU1-1 (lane A-5) — the recovery cursor's OWN stable cell.
///
/// Separate from the accounting cell (MemoryId 20) by ruling: two unrelated
/// concerns in one cell couple an accounting write to a cursor write, and the
/// cursor needs its own fail-closed semantics — **an absent region must never
/// read as scan-complete.**
const MEM_RECOVERY_CURSOR: MemoryId = MemoryId::new(21);

/// F2-REDACT: the redaction sweep's own KEY-BASED resumption cursor.
///
/// GRANTED by control (ledger 2026-08-22 17:21:27Z). `22` is FRESH — 0–21 are
/// allocated — so this is the registry's sanctioned APPEND, never a renumber or
/// a recycle; `docs/MEMORY_ID_REGISTRY.md` gains its row in this same change.
///
/// WHY A CURSOR IS REQUIRED. Redacted records stay in `TERMINAL_*_INDEX` until
/// day 30. A cursor-free window walk re-reads the already-redacted prefix at the
/// oldest edge every tick; once that prefix reaches `MAX_REDACT_SCAN_PER_TICK`
/// the sweep spends its whole budget re-reading redacted records and reaches
/// ZERO eligible ones, so later records age through the entire 7→30-day window
/// unredacted. The cursor walks PAST that prefix once per sweep.
///
/// WHY KEY-BASED AND NOT OFFSET-BASED (`CTO_RULING_A-5_cursor_keyed`, and the
/// same reasoning as `MEM_RECOVERY_CURSOR` above): pruning REMOVES entries, so
/// an offset shifts under the walk and silently skips records, while a key does
/// not. `range((Excluded(k), Unbounded))` is well-defined even when `k` has
/// since been pruned — which is exactly why a key survives a concurrent prune.
const MEM_REDACTION_CURSOR: MemoryId = MemoryId::new(22);

/// R-2 (C-30) — the batched `PrivateTransferFee` accrual, EAGER.
///
/// `[operations, insurance, staking]` totals for the CURRENT flush window. The
/// per-spend treasury notification is what made every private spend individually
/// recoverable from the treasury fee log (a source-labelled, retroactively
/// readable wall-clock timestamp per spend). The accrual replaces it: spends
/// add here, and one boundary-armed flush publishes the window aggregate.
///
/// **APPEND, not a renumber or a recycle:** 0–22 are allocated at base, so 23 is
/// FRESH; `docs/MEMORY_ID_REGISTRY.md` gains its row in this same change.
///
/// Its OWN cell, never folded into MemoryId 18 (`Scalars<3>`, grouped by the
/// fee-params epoch operation) nor into 24 (the flush window, changed by
/// governance): `Cell::set` rewrites the whole cell, and this one is mutated on
/// EVERY fee-bearing private spend. Grouping it with either would drag an
/// unrelated field into every spend's write.
const MEM_PENDING_FEE_ACCRUAL: MemoryId = MemoryId::new(23);

/// R-2 (C-30) — the flush-window governance parameter, EAGER.
